{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/493516-changelings-as-psychic-vampires","id":493516,"title":"Changelings as psychic vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-27T06:08:55-07:00","id":493516,"title":"Changelings as psychic vampires","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> So I like Changeling: the Lost. I'm very much interested in exploring the themes of surviving hardship, rebuilding oneself from the ashes, cycles of abuse, reclaiming one's life, etc.<br /> <br /> I also want my Changeling to be settled clearly in the genre of horror. I quite like the Vampire: the Requiem shade of horror, where vampires are essentially parasites feeding off humanity in a very literal sense - vampires drink life and kill people.<br /> <br /> I want something like that for Changeling, too, except in a more metaphorical sense.<br /> <br /> One of the few things I enjoyed about Changeling: the Dreaming is the way changelings replenished their Glamour reserves - by, essentially, taking away emotional energy from people.<br /> <br /> It's not hard to find a setting justification for changelings as psychic vampires. So you've got the Lost, once-humans irrevocably changed by their experiences in Faerie, a place that is nothing like the world of humans. They come back not quite complete. Parts of their humanity have been taken away, and there's nothing left to fill that gap. Changelings now need to fill that gap, feeding on human emotions.<br /> <br /> I'm still unsure how to implement all of this in terms of systems. I want the changeling method of consuming emotional energy to be a process that takes something away from the target (victim), leaving him drained, except on a more metaphorical layer than vampires drinking blood.<br /> <br /> My first thought: <br /> Feeding on Glamour created by people feeling strong emotions works as usual. The human loses one point of willpower for every two points of Glamour gained. Should there be no willpower left, the human takes one point of lethal damage for every four points of Glamour stolen.<br /> <br /> The one point of Glamour gained when feeding on the signature emotion as per one's Court is always free, meaning that it doesn't cause the human damage.<br /> <br /> Simple, but .. inelegant. I somehow want additional factors like derangements and, possibly, Morality to figure into the equation too.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> <span style=\"color:#777777\"> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </span><br /> </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T09:53:56-07:00","id":493705,"title":"","content":"Merge the emotion-harvesting regains with the pledge-boon regains and make losing Glamour create a temporary connection that gives the victim the maluses of a sanction scaled to the loss (so losing a bit of Glamour gives you a lesser sanction and it gets worse from there).<br /> <br /> Changelings can offset this ill fortune by gaining Glamour from a mortal (passing the penalty further down the line) or by using the features of the Hedge, which reverse this relationship (so gaining Glamour from Hedge bounty will offset the one curse but give you another until, say, you can get out, while losing more Glamour to the Thorns will bleed off the curse).<br /> <br /> Harvesting from dreams instills the madness of Arcadia in dreamer and changeling, which refills your Glamour pool completely but gives you a mild derangement that lasts [dreamer's Morality] nights and gives the dreamer a Morality-1 breaking point (two dice) whose failure results in the corresponding severe derangement for [10-new Morality] nights.<br /> <br /> An incredibly rough proposition, but there it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}